# Configuration for backup.sh / restore.sh.
#
# Copy to /opt/devplat/backup.env, fill in, then lock it down:
#   chown root:root /opt/devplat/backup.env && chmod 600 /opt/devplat/backup.env
#
# It holds the passphrase that decrypts every backup you own. Anyone who can
# read this file plus reach Swiss Backup has the whole database.

# --- rclone remote --------------------------------------------------------
# The section name in ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf. Infomaniak's emailed file
# calls it [sb_project_SBI-XX000000]; if you renamed it to [swissbackup] (the
# FAQ suggests this), put that name here instead.
RCLONE_REMOTE=swissbackup

# Container plus path inside the Swiss Backup device. "default" is the
# container Infomaniak creates; the subfolder keeps database dumps separate
# from anything else you ever back up to the same device.
RCLONE_PATH=default/postgres

# --- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the VPS's compose file and the name of the Postgres service in it.
# The dump runs inside that container, so Postgres stays internal-only.
COMPOSE_FILE=/opt/devplat/docker-compose.yml
POSTGRES_SERVICE=postgres
POSTGRES_USER=devplat
POSTGRES_DB=devplat

# --- Encryption -----------------------------------------------------------
# The dump is encrypted before it leaves the machine. This is not paranoia:
# the database holds bcrypt hashes, API token hashes, and — because TOTP is
# symmetric and has to stay verifiable — every enrolled user's live 2FA
# secret. That must not sit readable in a third party's object storage.
#
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 48
#
# STORE THIS IN YOUR PASSWORD MANAGER TOO. If this file dies with the VPS and
# the passphrase exists nowhere else, every backup you have is noise.
BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=CHANGE_ME

# --- Retention ------------------------------------------------------------
# Days to keep remote dumps. Swiss Backup bills by volume; a compressed dump
# of this schema is small, so 30 is cheap. Note this is deletion by age, not
# `rclone sync` — see the comment in backup.sh for why that distinction
# matters a great deal.
RETENTION_DAYS=30

# --- Reporting (optional but strongly recommended) ------------------------
# The API records each run so the admin dashboard can show backup freshness
# and alert when backups stop. Without it, a backup that silently stopped
# working four months ago looks exactly like one that works.
# Must match BACKUP_REPORT_TOKEN in the backend's .env.
API_URL=https://api.devplat.ch
BACKUP_REPORT_TOKEN=
